function k08InstallTransRightsQuestion(){
  k08SetReactiveQuestion(26,
    'October 2008: At a televised town hall, a college student asks about discrimination against transgender Americans. Most national politicians barely use the word “transgender” in public, but you have spoken for years about protections based on gender identity. Republicans immediately call the position proof that you are far outside the cultural mainstream. How do you answer?',
    [101,102,103,104],
    [
      'Do not hedge. Transgender Americans deserve the same civil-rights protections as anyone else, including explicit federal protection against discrimination. A right does not become optional because polling is behind it.',
      'Defend nondiscrimination clearly, but keep the answer narrow: nobody should lose a job, a home, or equal protection because of who they are. Do not turn this into a catalogue of new federal mandates.',
      'Say the country is still working through these questions. Support basic nondiscrimination while leaving many specific rules to states, courts, and local governments for now.',
      'Go further. This is exactly when leadership matters: promise a comprehensive federal gender-identity civil-rights agenda and accuse both parties of cowardice for refusing to say so.'
    ],
    [-.010,.026,.014,-.032],
    [
      {progressiveTrust:2,publicPerception:-1,voterAnxiety:1},
      {publicPerception:2,partySupport:1,voterAnxiety:-1,progressiveTrust:0},
      {publicPerception:1,voterAnxiety:-1,progressiveTrust:-2},
      {progressiveTrust:3,partySupport:-1,publicPerception:-2,voterAnxiety:2}
    ],
    [
      'There is no ambiguity, and activists are proud of it. The problem is temporal as much as ideological: in 2008 you are asking millions of voters to process a civil-rights argument the political mainstream has scarcely begun discussing.',
      'This is still well left of most national politicians, but it sounds like a familiar equal-protection argument rather than an invitation to fight every cultural battle at once. You remain progressive while lowering the temperature.',
      'Moderates are reassured, but LGBT activists immediately notice the retreat. You have not abandoned nondiscrimination, though you have moved your electoral posture noticeably closer to the center.',
      'The answer is years ahead of the national conversation and makes that fact impossible to miss. The movement loves the courage; culturally moderate voters in the Midwest and Appalachia recoil.'
    ]
  );
}
