  function install25(){
    const opp=nominee();
    set(25,
      `The ${opp} campaign has produced the simplest and perhaps most effective attack ad of the fall. Grainy footage from the 2007 Democratic debate shows you acknowledging that you once saw an unidentified flying object at Shirley MacLaine's home. It cuts to several unconventional proposals and then to black: "DENNIS KUCINICH. PRESIDENT?" Cable news is looping it. What do you say?`,
      [
        "A UFO means unidentified flying object. I saw something I couldn't identify. I never said Martians landed in Shirley MacLaine's yard, and I'm not going to let an attack ad rewrite what I actually said.",
        "Look, I saw something in the sky years ago that I couldn't identify. That is the entire story. We are in the middle of a financial crisis, and I am not going to spend the week helping the Republican campaign turn a light in the sky into a governing philosophy.",
        "Other people were there. If reporters are determined to spend time on this, they can ask the witnesses what they saw instead of acting as though I announced an alien invasion.",
        `I'd rather have seen a UFO than looked at the Bush administration for eight years and concluded the country needed more of the same. If ${opp} wants to have some fun with this, I can have some fun too.`
      ],
      [-.024,-.020,-.042,-.030],
      [
        {voterAnxiety:2,publicPerception:-1,mediaRelationship:-1},
        {voterAnxiety:2,publicPerception:-2},
        {voterAnxiety:3,publicPerception:-2,mediaRelationship:-2},
        {voterAnxiety:2,publicPerception:-1,progressiveTrust:1}
      ],
      [
        "Technically impeccable. Politically, you have now spent another news cycle explaining the definition of UFO. The ad keeps running.",
        "This is the least damaging exit available. You acknowledge exactly what happened, refuse to embellish it, and try to drag the conversation back to the economy. The footage does not disappear, but the story finally has somewhere to go.",
        "This is how a weird anecdote becomes an investigation. Reporters start calling everyone who was at the house, cable panels debate witness credibility, and the words SHIRLEY MACLAINE remain on screen for another forty-eight hours.",
        `The room laughs, and even some reporters admit the Bush line is funny. Unfortunately, funny means replayable. The ${opp} campaign gets another day of free UFO footage and you get another day of explaining why the joke should not be taken literally.`
      ]
    );
  }

